# Inbound agents for which post-call job creation is DISABLED (comma-separated
# agent_ids). For these agents (e.g. office-hours / after-hours) the ServiceTrade
# job is decided post the outbound dispatch call and only if  the technician approves it — never auto-created post-call by the webhook.
# Currently populated with the Adaptive Climate and Total Fire and Security agents.
# Placeholders below — get the real ids from `vercel env ls` / the Vercel dashboard.
# Adding an agent_id here removes ALL job-booking paths for that agent.
POSTCALL_JOB_DISABLED_AGENT_IDS="agent_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx,agent_yyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyy,agent_zzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzz"

# ADAPTIVE CLIMATE ONLY — no other tenant has a sheet in the loop.
# Every inbound call gets a row in the tracking sheet; once the job outcome is
# known that same row is updated in place, so one row tells the whole story of a
# call (caller, escalation trail, job created?, job number). That closing update
# is what this URL enables — it exists for observability.
#
# Adaptive Climates Apps Script web-app /exec URL. The outbound post-call webhook
# (/webhook/retell-outbound) POSTs the job result here (action:"job_update") so the
# escalation sheet row is updated with is_job_created / job_number / outcome.
# Use the same /exec value that the Vercel ADAPTIVE_EXEC_URL points at.
ADAPTIVE_SHEET_EXEC_URL=""

# ADAPTIVE CLIMATE ONLY — agents allowed to trigger the consolidated escalation
# email via POST /st-escalation-complete.
#
# The Apps Script owns escalation state, so it decides WHEN an emergency is over and
# POSTs the finished row here; this service decides HOW to email it, resolving
# recipients and the send/fail toggles from that agent's servicetrade_tokens row
# (emailto / ccmail / send_job_email / send_job_fail_email). One email per emergency,
# carrying the job outcome, job number and the full escalation trail.
#
# This is the ONLY thing standing between that endpoint and another tenant: an
# agent_id not listed here is rejected with "agent_not_enabled" and no email is sent.
# Tenants whose jobs are created on the inbound post-call path email through their own
# route and must never appear here.

# Value is the OUTBOUND dispatch agent id — the same one the Apps Script sends as
# CONFIG.RETELL_AGENT_ID. The two must match or every notification is rejected.
# If unset, falls back to the Adaptive outbound agent id hardcoded in
# src/config/environment.js.
ESCALATION_EMAIL_AGENT_IDS="agent_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"

# ADAPTIVE CLIMATE ONLY — POST /st-inbound-lookup.
#
# Retell's inbound-call webhook, configured PER PHONE NUMBER in the Retell dashboard
# (not on the agent). It fires before the agent speaks, and what the endpoint returns
# becomes dynamic variables on the call: st_location_found, st_location_status,
# st_location_name, st_location_address, st_lookup_ok.
#
# Purpose is advisory. It lets the agent CONFIRM a known caller's address instead of
# interrogating them for it. It never rejects a call and never blocks anything — an
# inactive location is dispatched exactly like an active one.
#
# INBOUND agent ids allowed to use the route. Anything else gets empty variables.
# Defaults to the three Adaptive inbound agents (main router, office, after-hours).
INBOUND_LOOKUP_AGENT_IDS="agent_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx,agent_yyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyy"

# Whose servicetrade_tokens row the lookup authenticates with. NOT the inbound agent:
# for Adaptive the ServiceTrade config lives on the OUTBOUND dispatch agent, the same
# row /st-match-location and post-call job creation resolve. Defaults to that agent.
INBOUND_LOOKUP_ST_AGENT_ID="agent_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"

# NOTE: The outbound post-call webhook (/webhook/retell-outbound) resolves the
# ServiceTrade config from the OUTBOUND dispatch agent's OWN id (call.agent_id) —
# each outbound agent has its own servicetrade_tokens + servicetrade_job_configs
# row (per tenant). There is intentionally no global default agent id: a missing
# row fails loudly rather than creating a job under the wrong ServiceTrade account.

# Recipients of internal error/alert emails (sendInternalAlert) — comma or
# semicolon separated. If unset, falls back to the built-in team list in
# src/config/environment.js.
INTERNAL_ALERT_RECIPIENTS="alerts.one@example.com,alerts.two@example.com"


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ServiceTrade location mirror (read side)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `servicetrade_locations` is WRITTEN by a Supabase Edge Function on an hourly
# pg_cron schedule — supabase/functions/sync-locations, scheduled by
# db/supabase-sync-locations-cron.sql. This service never writes it.
#
# It READS the mirror as the caller-phone fallback when ServiceTrade is unreachable,
# and needs the tenant mapping to know whose rows to read. There is no CRON_SECRET:
# the Edge Function's own JWT verification handles auth, and pg_cron sends the
# project's existing service-role key.

# Which agents are mirrored — just the agent id the rows are keyed by. Everything
# else is derived, so there is nothing else to keep correct:
#   company_id  — read off the rows already stored for that agent (public.companies
#                 disagrees with the mirror for 3 of 5 agents, so it is not a source)
#   the session — found via the shared `st_username` on servicetrade_tokens; the
#                 Adaptive inbound and outbound agents authenticate as the same
#                 ServiceTrade user
#
# Keep this in step with the Edge Function's own secret:
#   supabase secrets set LOCATION_SYNC_AGENT_IDS="..."
#
# Defaults to the Adaptive Climates inbound agent.
LOCATION_SYNC_AGENT_IDS="agent_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SUPABASE_URL plus a key. Most of this service reads through src/config/database.js,
# which accepts SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, SUPABASE_KEY or SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, in that
# order of preference.
#
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY is required SPECIFICALLY, not just "one of the three", by
# src/services/escalationStore.js — the Adaptive escalation record. `escalation_chains`
# has RLS enabled with no policy, so an anon key is denied outright.
#
# If it is missing, the mirror disables itself with a console warning and NOTHING ELSE
# BREAKS: escalations keep running, jobs keep being created, and the dashboard simply
# never shows an escalation. That is a quiet failure worth checking for deliberately
# after a deploy — look for "[escalation-store] ... dashboard mirror disabled".
SUPABASE_URL=""
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=""
